.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::NumIntegral_dudn_op_u_dS_InterFace_w_dimM1_Region< dim >"Use to apply a Robin type (flux) boundary condition coupling the sides of the Interface with a lower-dimensional region in the middle between them\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
use for transient computations involving fractures
.RE
.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
SKM 
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
18/8/22 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> \fBcsmp::NumIntegral_dudn_op_u_dS_InterFace_w_dimM1_Region\fP< dim >::NumIntegral_dudn_op_u_dS_InterFace_w_dimM1_Region (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & model, const char * oper, const char * basic, const char * test, double dt)"
Constructor gets the finite element types that \fBNumIntegral_dudn_op_u_dS_InterFace_w_dimM1_Region\fP needs to turn the \fBInterFace\fP into the equivalent of a volumetric element from the \fBFiniteElementManager\fP\&. Since InterFaces can either be triangles or quadrilaterals, their extruded volumetric pendants are prism and hexahedral elements\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
the variable 'thickness' needs to be defined on the \fBInterFace\fP, else the pde operator will not work\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
